The bug violating the requirements in [`requirement.feature`](file:///Users/nothing/prometheus_workdir_microstudy/math_63_group_c_fix/requirement.feature) was located in [`MathUtils.java`](file:///Users/nothing/prometheus_workdir_microstudy/math_63_group_c_fix/src/main/java/org/apache/commons/math/util/MathUtils.java#L416-L418).

### Cause
In `MathUtils.equals(double x, double y)`:
```java
public static boolean equals(double x, double y) {
    return (Double.isNaN(x) && Double.isNaN(y)) || x == y;
}
```
This method erroneously considered two `Double.NaN` values to be equal. Consequently, both `equals(double, double)` and `equals(double[], double[])` returned `true` when comparing `Double.NaN` values, violating the requirement.

### Solution
Updated `MathUtils.equals(double, double)` to delegate to `equals(x, y, 1)`:
```java
public static boolean equals(double x, double y) {
    return equals(x, y, 1);
}
```

The patch containing only source code modifications has been saved to [`negative_fix.patch`](file:///Users/nothing/prometheus_workdir_microstudy/math_63_group_c_fix/negative_fix.patch). All verification tests now pass successfully.
